The documentation here is slightly ambiguous. While `0` in the configuration triggers a fallback to the pipeline timeout (as noted on line 77), this comment suggests `0` directly means "no timeout". This is only true if the fallback `PipelineTimeout()` also returns `0`. It would be clearer to specify that the fallback occurs when the value is `0` and that a resulting duration of `0` implies no timeout.

```suggestion
// Uses features.export_timeout_ms when set (must be > 0); otherwise falls back to PipelineTimeout().
// A resulting duration of 0 means no timeout (only shutdown cancels).
```
